  "trich": "The CB750 is an air-cooled, transverse, in-line-four-cylinder-engine motorcycles made by Honda over several generations for year models 1969–2008 with an upright, or standard, riding posture. It is often called the original Universal Japanese Motorcycle (UJM) and also is regarded as the first motorcycle to be called a \"superbike\". The CR750 is the associated works racer.",
